<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sant Andreu de Sureda</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saint-André-de-Sorède</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sant Andreu de Sureda, in French Saint-André-de-Sorède, is a former Benedictine abbey in the foothills of the Albères in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Its church has a carved marble lintel of the early 11th century, made by the same workshop as the dated lintel of nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sant-genis-de-fontanes">Sant Genís de Fontanes</a>, among the earliest works of Romanesque sculpture.</p></div>
